======================================================================
PART C: TOURNAMENT = BASIS FOR so(n) (HYP-786)
======================================================================

  --- n=3 ---
  dim(so(3)) = 3
  Bracket test: 3 basis elements, 27 Jacobi tests
  Killing form diagonal: {-2}
  Expected: -2 (= -2*(n-2))
  Match: True
  INTERPRETATION: Tournament on 3 vertices = choice of orientation
  for the 3 generators of so(3). ALL tournaments give the SAME
  abstract Lie algebra, just with different signed basis elements.

  --- n=4 ---
  dim(so(4)) = 6
  Bracket test: 6 basis elements, 125 Jacobi tests
  Killing form diagonal: {-4}
  Expected: -4 (= -2*(n-2))
  Match: True
  INTERPRETATION: Tournament on 4 vertices = choice of orientation
  for the 6 generators of so(4). ALL tournaments give the SAME
  abstract Lie algebra, just with different signed basis elements.

  --- n=5 ---
  dim(so(5)) = 10
  Bracket test: 10 basis elements, 125 Jacobi tests
  Killing form diagonal: {-6}
  Expected: -6 (= -2*(n-2))
  Match: True
  INTERPRETATION: Tournament on 5 vertices = choice of orientation
  for the 10 generators of so(5). ALL tournaments give the SAME
  abstract Lie algebra, just with different signed basis elements.

======================================================================
PART D: SUPER ORTHOGONALITY — ENTANGLEMENT OF LEVELS
======================================================================

  LEVEL 0 (Statistical):
  H is complement-symmetric: H(T) = H(T^op) for all T
  Any antisymmetric function f (f(T^op) = -f(T)) is orthogonal to H

  LEVEL 1 (Walsh):
  H Walsh support: 91 even-weight, 0 odd-weight
  H is purely even-weight: True

  LEVEL 2 (Algebraic):
  THM-076: Walsh amplitudes depend ONLY on (r, k) of the monomial S
  This is forced by C(m,j) * j! * (m-j)! = m! (constant-term identity)
  Distinct |Walsh amplitudes| for H: 3
    |hat{H}| = 0.125000: 60 monomials
    |hat{H}| = 0.750000: 30 monomials
    |hat{H}| = 7.500000: 1 monomials

  LEVEL 3 (Homological):
  beta_2 = 0 for ALL tournaments (THM-108)
  This means: dim(ker d_2) = dim(im d_3) EXACTLY for all T
  The 2-boundary space saturates the 2-cycle space

  LEVEL 4 (Super Orthogonality):
  The four levels are NOT independent. Entanglements:

  [L0 <-> L1]: Complement symmetry (L0) forces Walsh parity (L1)
    H(T) = H(T^op) implies hat{H}[S] = 0 for odd-weight S

  [L1 <-> L2]: Walsh parity (L1) + OCF (L2) forces amplitude formula
    The factorization H = I(Omega,2) decomposes in Walsh space
    Each degree contributes 2^r*(n-2k)!/2^(n-1) independently

  [L2 <-> L3]: OCF (L2) + path homology (L3) are DUAL
    H = I(Omega,2) counts cycle-disjoint collections
    beta_2 = 0 means 2-cycles are all boundaries of 3-chains
    Both are manifestations of: odd cycles generate the structure

  [L0 <-> L3]: Complement symmetry (L0) forces beta_2=0 (L3)?
    OPEN: Does H(T)=H(T^op) imply beta_2(T)=0?
    Tournament-specific: beta_2=0 uses completeness, not just symmetry

  ENTANGLEMENT MEASURE:
  Walsh parameters (non-zero coefficients): 91
  OCF parameters (alpha_k values): 2
  Combined effective parameters: 2 (OCF is more efficient)
  Redundancy ratio: 91 / 2 = 45.5
  This 46x redundancy IS the super orthogonality:
  the Walsh coefficients are 46x over-determined by OCF
